Z||000000||Galen||08-12-2001||07:24 PM||||Okie, I went out of town today about maybe 30 miles. It was a trip I made alot a few years ago. So anyways, I stopped at walmart and walked around a bit. Came back out to my car, and went to crank it.. turn the key.. nothing. I was like, okie this sucks. headlights, radio, fan everything worked. Just wouldn't start. So I figured maybe my battery was low enough that it would start but everything else would work. Walk back in and catch the TLE ppl just closing. Seeing as how I worked with em(the reason I made that trip alot) they decided they'd jump my car for me. Me & a friend of mine(wallyworld associate) got out to my car, I turn the key. Cranks right up. My question is, could this possibly be my starter going out or something else? The car had only been sitting for maybe 20 minutes when I came back out.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Ray</FONT> <FONT COLOR="gray">-</FONT> <FONT COLOR="purple">"With one drop of blood he realized his own mortallity, it was then he saw the true face of God. For he is not someone watching down on us, but he is in us." - Galen 2001</FONT>||||reg||5
